# The roadmap files below are machine-managed by harness roadmap tooling, and
# the schema requires each `- **Key:** value` field to be ONE physical line.
# Prettier's `proseWrap: "always"` wraps them, and harness reads only the first
# line and silently discards the rest — no error on either side. A shard + regen
# round-trip took the file from 40,525 bytes to 11,640 before this entry existed.
#
# This is not a style preference and it is not dead config. `.harness/hooks/
# quality-warner.js` runs `prettier --check` on every file written in this repo
# and blocks on violation, so without this line an agent cannot write a correct
# roadmap at all — the hook forces the broken shape.
#
# CAVEAT: prettier resolves this file relative to the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY.
# Run it from the repo root. From `ts/` (where the four gates run) an
# `npx prettier --write ../docs/roadmap.md` reflows every field as if this entry
# did not exist.
#
# `docs/roadmap.md` also depends on its `markdownlint-disable-file MD013`
# comment: docs-lint.yml lints every markdown file with no path filter and is a
# REQUIRED check, and the unwrapped file has 50 lines over 80 columns. The
# field-contract test asserts that comment is present for the same reason it
# asserts the fields are unwrapped.
#
# Removing an entry silently re-breaks that file. The guard that FAILS when it
# happens is ts/test/roadmap-field-contract.test.ts — and it DERIVES its file
# list from the `docs/roadmap*` entries below (#630), so the exempted set and
# guarded set are the same set mechanically rather than by instruction. Adding
# a line here enrols the file in the guard; there is no second list to update.
# If `harness roadmap shard` output is ever committed, add `docs/roadmap.d` and
# every shard is scanned. See docs/changes/roadmap-priority-and-field-contract/
# and AGENTS.md.
#
# docs/roadmap-archive.md is the same contract: scripts/roadmap-groom.mjs moves
# rows into it verbatim, so a row that is one-line-correct in docs/roadmap.md
# arrives one-line-correct here and prettier must not rewrap it. Measured
# 2026-08-08, before this entry: 60 of its 63 rows had a wrapped `Summary`,
# and `prettier --check` called the file clean while holding it that way.
docs/roadmap.md
